<ResourceDictionary xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">

  <!--
    Seed exceptions, not a palette. Three seeds in App.xaml generate every semantic role; the role
    below is the one the generator's recipe structurally cannot reach, so it is pinned back to the
    authored brand value. Colors.OverrideSource merges last and wins over the generated palette, and
    Uno.Themes rewrites the matching *Brush keys (and their hover/pressed/disabled variants) from
    these values.

    Both themes are declared on purpose: the brush resolver probes Light then Default, so a role
    given only a Default value would bleed its dark color into light.

    Why this one:
    - SecondaryColor — only the light PrimaryColor is the seed verbatim under SeedColorMode.Fidelity;
      Secondary and Tertiary are pinned to tone 40 in light. FitStart's energy orange sits well above
      tone 40, so the generated role comes back as a dark brown and loses the accent entirely.
  -->
  <ResourceDictionary.ThemeDictionaries>

    <ResourceDictionary x:Key="Light">
      <Color x:Key="SecondaryColor">#E07B1F</Color>
    </ResourceDictionary>

    <ResourceDictionary x:Key="Default">
      <Color x:Key="SecondaryColor">#FFB870</Color>
    </ResourceDictionary>

  </ResourceDictionary.ThemeDictionaries>
</ResourceDictionary>
